---
import LabsLayout from "../../layouts/labs.astro";
---

<LabsLayout title="Combined package — Querial Labs" active="combined">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-indigo-on-dark">Labs</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Combined package</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3">
                <code class="text-foreground">aw-lab-all</code> is one zip with every
                selected scenario pipeline and a union connection catalog. Use it when you
                want all six labs in a single import into the current project.
                Scenario F is included in the default <code class="text-foreground">-Combined</code> set.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <a href="/labs/adventureworks/downloads/aw-lab-all.zip" download
               class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-querial-indigo px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:opacity-90">
                Download aw-lab-all.zip
            </a>
            <a href="/labs/packing" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted/50">
                Rebuild with -Combined
            </a>
        </div>

        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <h2>What is inside</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Package code <code class="text-foreground">aw-lab-all</code>.</li>
                <li>Pipelines: <code class="text-foreground">aw_scenario_a</code> … <code class="text-foreground">aw_scenario_f</code> (when packed with the default scenario set).</li>
                <li>Catalog union: <code class="text-foreground">aw-source</code>, <code class="text-foreground">aw-sql-dest</code>, <code class="text-foreground">aw-pg-dest</code>. Same name with different providers is rejected at pack time.</li>
                <li>Each pipeline keeps its own connection allow-list from the original scenario.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Import</h2>
            <p>
                Same modal as a single scenario. Resolve the three stubs once. Success
                reports six pipelines. Overwrite drafts if you previously imported A–F
                separately (same pipeline codes). F still cannot be scheduled after import.
            </p>
            <p>
                Publish <strong class="text-foreground">each</strong> pipeline you intend
                to run. Create one Development deployment per pipeline (or start with A,
                then B). Do not assume one deployment covers the forest — a deployment
                binds one published version.
            </p>

            <h2>Rebuild a subset</h2>
            <pre class="rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>.\build-packages.ps1 -Combined -Scenarios A,B -Zip
# still writes scenario-a and scenario-b trees, plus aw-lab-all with only A and B</code></pre>

            <h2>When to prefer single zips</h2>
            <p>
                Teaching one topology: download that scenario zip so the project is not
                cluttered. Combined is for a shared lab project that will run all paths
                against the same three logical connections.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</LabsLayout>
